juvenile jokes gone wrong,

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:32.460
and has admitted to his
mistakes in the past.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.030
- I'm really sorry if I offended, hurt,

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:38.430
or disappointed anyone with all of this.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.110
- Unfortunately, some
right-wing communities

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.380
have adopted PewDiePie as a kind of mascot

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.270
in their movement, posting about him

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:46.190
in the neo-Nazi site the Daily Stormer,

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.140
and making lots of memes
promoting his content.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.190
This kind of third party
attributions reached a fever pitch

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.000
after the New Zealand mosque massacre

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.730
wehen the shooter
actually encouraged people

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.670
to quote, subscribe to PewDiePie,

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:00.210
as was part of the
internet meme at the time.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.330
- I think it's time to end

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.750
the subscribe to PewDiePie
movement or meme.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.890
- PewDiePie staunchly
maintains that he is not

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:07.860
a supporter of any right-wing causes,

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.480
but others have said that
PewDiePie has not done enough

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.310
to distance himself from
these various groups.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.280
Generally, PewDiePie has reiterated that

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.480
his overall stance is it's just a joke

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.131
and it's all a parody,
which takes us to T-Series.

00:03:22.131 --> 00:03:24.950
The latest issue involving
PewDiePie's sense of humor

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.910
involves the Indian
record company T-Series,

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:31.090
which has a huge following
on YouTube in its own right.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:33.196
As of the time of this video,

00:03:33.196 --> 00:03:36.840
the Indian record label
T-Series has the biggest

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.930
YouTube channel in the entire world,

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.430
which recently PewDiePie's channel

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.770
with over 97 million
subscribers and counting.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.590
It looks like T-Series is going to be

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:49.390
the first channel to reach
100 million subscribers

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.357
in the entire world.

00:03:50.357 --> 00:03:53.230
After T-Series surpassed
PewDiePie in followers,

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.860
he responded with two
satirical diss tracks,

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.390
one called Congratulations,

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.460
and the other called
called (bleep) Lasagna.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.643
- T-Series, yeah!

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.707
- We are definitely going
to have to bleep out

00:04:03.707 --> 00:04:05.800
(bleep) Lasagna, because (bleep) Lasagna

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.130
is totally inappropriate.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:09.980
T-Series was not amused by the two videos.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.583
The company filed a
lawsuit in Indian court

00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:14.920
alleging that the videos were disparaging,

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.330
defamatory, racist, and offensive.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.631
Back in October of 2018,
PewDiePie apologized

00:04:20.631 --> 00:04:22.830
for the tracks in his typical fashion,

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.790
claiming that it was just a joke

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.680
and removed the tracks for a while.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.055
When the tracks remained on the channel,

00:04:29.055 --> 00:04:31.417
T-Series filed for an injunction

00:04:31.417 --> 00:04:34.900
in the Indian legal system
to get the videos taken down.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.400
So what did PewDiePie
say to get into trouble?

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.630
Well, the track Congratulations
is a tongue-in-cheek

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.750
music video that purports
to congratulate T-Series

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.412
on surpassing PewDiePie's
channel in number of subscribers,

00:04:47.412 --> 00:04:50.470
but here is what the song actually says.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.760
PewDiePie accuses them
of once being a purveyor

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.900
of pirated songs and videos,

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.940
he says that T-Series sent
him a defamation letter,

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.050
he insinuates that they have
ties to the Indian mafia,

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.950
he asserts that he has never defamed them

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.830
and that his opinion isn't defamation,

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:06.930
saying for legal reasons that's a joke.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.360
Popular YouTuber Boy in a
Band, who co-wrote the song,

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.180
goes into great detail about
the songwriting process.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.760
- Hi, I'm Dave from Boy in a Band,

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.270
and recently me and my friend
Roomie have made a song

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.903
with PewDiePie.
(crowd murmuring)

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.990
Whoa, whoa, whoa, calm down fellas.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.700
- It's definitely worth
a look on his channel,

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.470
and as a purported example
of what isn't defamation,

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.650
he says that Indians have
poo poo in the brains,

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.070
still not defamation.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.740
PewDiePie actually nails the issue

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:38.960
with that last lyric,
it's still not defamation.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.060
Or does he?

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.260
What counts as defamation?

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:45.254
Well first, let's talk about
defamation under US law.

00:05:45.254 --> 00:05:48.640
Defamation is the communication
of a false statement

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.530
that harms a person or
organization's reputation.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.370
Like the United States,
India's legal system

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.560
is based on English common law,

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:58.280
but America, India, and
the UK approach defamation

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:00.450
in completely different ways.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.670
The law of defamation is concerned
with stopping publication

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.440
of statements that injure
a person's reputation.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.550
This law comes from the
common law of England,

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.360
where Alfred the Great once announced that

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:14.300
public slander was to be
compensated with no lighter penalty

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:17.120
than the cutting off of
the slanderer's tongue.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.750
Although we aren't cutting
out anyone's tongue

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:22.300
for defamation these days,
there are now civil penalties

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.220
for defamation in the United States.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:26.090
Some legal commentators
have noted that all

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.460
American freedoms begin
with freedom of speech,

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:30.380
and over the years,
American law has developed

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:33.450
a doctrine of defamation
that tries to balance harm

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.780
to someone's reputation
with the anti-censorship

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.470
tradition of the first amendment.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:39.200
So let's do a quick review of how to

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.550
prove defamation in America.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:43.082
There are two kinds of
defamation historically,

00:06:43.082 --> 00:06:45.796
slander is defamation
by spoken word alone,

00:06:45.796 --> 00:06:49.860
whereas libel is defamation by
written word, video, or song.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.760
But in the modern context, there
isn't much differentiation,

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.890
it's basically all defamation.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.970
A communication may be
considered defamatory

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.580
if it, quote, tends to
so harm the reputation

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:02.240
of another as to lower
him in the estimation

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:04.480
of the community or to deter third persons

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.023
from associating with him.

00:07:06.023 --> 00:07:10.075
To prove defamation, the
defendant must show three things.

00:07:10.075 --> 00:07:12.580
The defendant knowingly
or negligently made

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:16.362
a false and defamatory
statement of verifiable fact

00:07:16.362 --> 00:07:18.230
concerning the plaintiff.

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.400
The defendant made an
unprivileged publication

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.980
to a third party, and the publisher acted

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:26.000
at least negligently in
publishing the communication.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.870
The statement must be, of course, untrue

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:29.830
and harmful to one's reputation.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.130
The defendant can defend him or herself

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.560
by claiming that the
statements are literally true,

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.220
but the burden proof is on the person

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.760
who says the statements
are defamatory to show

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.990
that the statements are actually false.

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:42.960
American law has an even higher standard

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.988
when the plaintiff is a public figure.

00:07:44.988 --> 00:07:47.180
When the statements
involve a public figure,

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:49.550
it doesn't matter if
they happen to be false.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:52.150
In those cases, a plaintiff must also show

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.710
that whoever made the statement did so

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:56.020
with what's called actual malice.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:58.280
By choosing this standard,
American law has chosen

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:00.838
to tip the balance in
favor of free speech.

00:08:00.838 --> 00:08:03.050
India, on the other hand, tips the balance

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:06.510
in favor of protecting the
person or entity's reputation.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.470
Mind you, I am not an Indian lawyer,

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:10.880
this is merely my understanding
based on my research

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.890
as an outsider looking
in, so take my statements

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:15.450
with a grain of salt.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:18.520
So let's talk about
defamation under Indian law.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:21.090
The Indian constitution
protects freedom of speech

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:23.508
under Article 19 to that constitution,

00:08:23.508 --> 00:08:25.710
however defamation is an exception

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.270
to the general protections of free speech.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.450
India makes a person's
reputation as a key aspect

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:34.300
of the right to life,
which is also guaranteed

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.110
under the Indian constitution.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.500
India's definition of
defamation is the, quote,

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.780
publication of a statement which reflects

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:43.833
on a person's reputation and
tends to lower him or her

00:08:43.833 --> 00:08:46.850
in the estimation of
right-thinking members of society

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:51.032
generally or tends to make
them shun or avoid him or her.

00:08:51.032 --> 00:08:53.658
In India, defamation can be both a civil

00:08:53.658 --> 00:08:55.950
and criminal cause of action.

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.900
India's actually one of the few countries

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:00.630
that makes defamation a criminal offense.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:02.860
India's penal code criminalizes any speech

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.820
that quote, promotes enmity
between different groups

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.414
on grounds of religion,
race, place of birth,

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:10.218
resident, and language.

00:09:10.218 --> 00:09:13.650
Indian penal code section
499 makes defamation a crime

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.040
punishable by up to two years in prison.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.180
It defines defamation as
a statement concerning

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.690
any person intending to harm
or knowing or having reason

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.220
to believe that his statement will harm

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:24.340
the person's reputation.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:27.110
The existence of criminal
penalties for defamatory speech

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:30.030
contributes to an overall
environment that is

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.880
on balance chilling to free speech.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.070
If you fear potential jail, after all,

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.530
you're going to think twice
about what you publish.

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.473
While there are several
exceptions to section 499,

00:09:39.473 --> 00:09:42.668
truth is not always one
of those exceptions,

00:09:42.668 --> 00:09:45.170
and the civil claim in India is similar.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.830
Truth is a defense only if the statement

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:48.910
was made for the public good.

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:50.970
If the statement was true but was intended

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:52.870
to hurt someone's reputation,

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:56.190
then under Indian law,
defamation still applies.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:58.470
Defamation in India
includes statements made

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:02.100
against corporations, people,
and even the deceased as well.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.570
Defamation can include
things which are just jokes.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:08.550
The Indian law states that
an imputation in form of

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.010
an alternative or expressed ironically,

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.048
may amount to defamation.

00:10:13.048 --> 00:10:15.508
So looking at PewDiePie's case,

00:10:15.508 --> 00:10:19.090
PewDiePie's defense that
his videos are just jokes

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.128
would work pretty well in the US.

00:10:21.128 --> 00:10:24.620
Satire and parody are good
defenses to defamation.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:27.200
Satire can be a sharp political critique,

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:30.943
and such commentary is well
within speech rights in the US.

00:10:30.943 --> 00:10:32.850
Parody makes light of a situation,

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:35.050
and although it's not as
sharpy critical as satire,

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.040
parody is also a valid defense
to charges of defamation.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.430
When it comes to parody, as
long as the false statement

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:42.450
is so over-the-top and ridiculous

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.410
that no one would take it seriously,

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.860
then that defense is likely to succeed.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.930
And that's also what
happened in the infamous case

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.550
of Jerry Falwell versus Hustler magazine.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.290
When Hustler magazine
published a parody account

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.063
of Jerry Falwell's first sexual encounter,

00:10:57.063 --> 00:10:59.670
Falwell sued the magazine for defamation.

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:02.210
Hustler and its owner
Larry Flynt prevailed

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:04.400
because no reasonable
person would have considered

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:08.222
the humorous and periodic
article to be a true account

00:11:08.222 --> 00:11:10.890
of Falwell's private life.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:13.920
So the up shot of all of this
is that the same YouTube video

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:17.520
that could be considered
defamatory in India is almost

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:19.890
certainly acceptable free
speech in the United States.

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:22.110
Although the India High
Court ruled that YouTube

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.820
had to block PewDiePie's videos in India,

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.630
